  "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=2x+3,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSuppose we wish to approximate the solution using the following numerical method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & =(x{y}^{\u2032}+{y}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={x}^{2}+3x,$ compute the local truncation error, ${\u03c4}_{1},$ for the first step starting at $x=0$ with step size $\u0394x=0.1.$\n\n${\u03c4}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}",
